- Check the left subtree; if it reports −2, return −2
- Check the right subtree; if it reports −2, return −2
- If the two heights differ by more than 1, return −2
- Otherwise return 1 + the larger of the two heights
hint: The base case comes first.
hint: A node can only compare heights once it has both of them.
